    AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER
    LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING
    FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER
    DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.

    qore#6930: a RestClient on http_version "auto" that had upgraded to HTTP/3 kept sending on its QUIC connection
    after the server restarted, as a server process that is killed sends no CONNECTION_CLOSE and a new one knows
    nothing of the connection, and the request failed with HTTP3-IDLE-CLOSE when the idle timer expired (75 s).  The
    connection is now closed when the server sends nothing, not even an acknowledgement, within the connect timeout of
    the request (HTTP3-PEER-UNRESPONSIVE); an idempotent request is repeated once on a new connection, while another
    one, which the old server may have processed before it went away, raises the error, and the next request takes a
    new connection.  The server is stopped as a killed one is with dbg_quic_silent_server_close() (debug
    builds): it sends no GOAWAY and no CONNECTION_CLOSE.
*/

%modern

%prepend-module-path "${SCRIPT_DIR}/../../../../qlib"
%requires Util
%requires QUnit
%requires Logger
%requires HttpServerUtil
%requires HttpServer
%requires RestClient
%requires json

%exec-class RestClientH3ServerRestartTest

#! The bound on a blocking wait: a hang guard only, never a timing assertion
const HangGuard = 60s;

#! The connect timeout of the client, which bounds the wait for a server that does not answer a request
const ConnectTimeout = 1s;

